<title>HONG KONG: New Island interim net rises 70 percent.</title>
<headline>New Island interim net rises 70 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   18.0   vs  10.6 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    4.0    vs  3.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil    vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    39.58  vs  23.25</p>
<p>    Turnover		     209.07 vs  166.54</p>
<p>    Company name		 New Island Printing Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  January 2-7, 1997</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   January 10</p>
<p>NOTE - New Island is a packaging maker.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings has been adjusted for the bonus issue of shares approved on September 20, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
